# CODEOWNERS — cross-team file-ownership boundary (seed K.10, Pipeline v2.1 Day-1 baseline)
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# When the app team and DevOps share one repo, the files DevOps customizes for the
# production build/deploy (Dockerfile, /deploy/**, CI/CD config) are a cross-TEAM
# contract surface. A feature branch carrying its own copy of these files will silently
# overwrite DevOps's customizations on merge, and the next CI build ships the wrong
# image (the EF-AI S34 "deployed pod still ran the old code" hour). Marking the boundary
# here means GitHub auto-requests the owning team's review on any PR that touches them,
# and (with branch protection "Require review from Code Owners") can require their
# approval before merge.
#
# SETUP (Stage 0):
#   1. Replace <DEVOPS_HANDLE> with the real team/user, e.g. @your-org/devops.
#      The owner MUST have write access to the repo (GitHub requirement).
#   2. In repo Settings -> Branches (or a ruleset), enable
#      "Require review from Code Owners" on the protected branch.
#   3. If this is a solo / no-DevOps repo, delete the build/deploy lines below
#      rather than leaving a fake owner — an unmatched/invalid owner assigns no one.
#
# SYNTAX: <path-pattern>  <owner1> [owner2 ...]  (last matching pattern wins)
# Paths are case-sensitive. `!` negation and `[ ]` ranges are NOT supported here.

# ---- M6-W4 FINDING, 2026-08-17: these owners are PLACEHOLDERS and assign nobody ----
# `<DEVOPS_HANDLE>` is not a GitHub handle, so every rule below matches a pattern and requests
# review from no one. This file's own SETUP note says a solo repo should DELETE these lines rather
# than leave a fake owner, "because an unmatched/invalid owner assigns no one" — which is exactly
# what has been true here since Stage 0. It is a control that reads as installed and is inert:
# the class this project has found four times this milestone.
#
# NOT deleted by the agent, because K.10 is a boundary and removing one is the owner's call. Two
# honest options at the milestone gate:
#   (a) solo repo -> delete the five rules below and keep this note as the record of why;
#   (b) a real reviewer exists -> replace the placeholder with their handle and enable
#       "Require review from Code Owners" on the protected branch, without which the file is
#       advisory whatever it says.
# Recorded as W-021.

# ---- DevOps-owned build & deploy surface (do not let an app-feature merge clobber) ----
/Dockerfile          <DEVOPS_HANDLE>
/.dockerignore       <DEVOPS_HANDLE>
/deploy/             <DEVOPS_HANDLE>
/.github/workflows/  <DEVOPS_HANDLE>
/Makefile            <DEVOPS_HANDLE>

# ---- Protect the ownership boundary itself (so it can't be quietly edited away) ----
/.github/CODEOWNERS  <DEVOPS_HANDLE>

# ---- (Optional) app-team default owner for everything else ----
# *                  <APP_TEAM_HANDLE>
